---

---

<span id="start-page-title" class="anchor-alias" aria-hidden="true"></span><span
  id="start-page-close-title"
  class="anchor-alias"
  aria-hidden="true"></span>
<section
  class="feature-copy-grid feature-copy-grid--top"
  aria-labelledby="start-page-section-0"
>
  <div>
    <h2 id="start-page-section-0">
      A different starting point, whenever you want.
    </h2>
  </div>
  <div class="feature-copy-list">
    <article>
      <h3>Billboard</h3><p>
        A large clock, your weekly blocked-request total, frequently visited
        sites, and your named groups. Billboard is the default; change layouts
        from the start-page footer or Settings → General.
      </p>
    </article>
    <article>
      <h3>Ledger</h3><p>
        A simple list of Favorites and named groups. When you opt into sharing
        tabs, Ledger also shows tabs from your other devices.
      </p>
    </article>
    <article>
      <h3>Shelf</h3><p>
        Favorites as tiles, with named groups and a weekly blocking total
        underneath.
      </p>
    </article>
    <article>
      <h3>Tally</h3><p>
        Favorites and groups beside a day-by-day chart of blocked requests this
        week.
      </p>
    </article>
  </div>
</section>
<section class="feature-copy-grid" aria-labelledby="start-page-section-1">
  <div>
    <h2 id="start-page-section-1">
      Your regular sites, a click away.
    </h2>
  </div>
  <div class="feature-copy-list">
    <article>
      <h3>Built from your own visits</h3><p>
        Billboard ranks ordinary browsing history on this device. Its site icons
        come from locally cached artwork; drawing the row makes no new request
        to those sites or a favicon service.
      </p>
    </article>
    <article>
      <h3>Hide a tile without erasing a visit</h3><p>
        Remove a site from Billboard when you do not want it there. That choice
        stays local and does not delete its history. Private tabs neither
        contribute to nor receive the history-derived row.
      </p>
    </article>
  </div>
</section>
<section class="feature-copy-grid" aria-labelledby="start-page-section-2">
  <div>
    <h2
      id="start-page-section-2"
    >
      Eight boards. A different Daily deal.
    </h2>
  </div>
  <div class="feature-copy-list">
    <article>
      <h3>Standalone Mahjong</h3><p>
        Open a standalone Mahjong solitaire table from any start-page footer.
        Your start page stays open while the game runs in its own managed tab.
      </p>
    </article>
    <article>
      <h3>A board with a solution</h3><p>
        Turtle, Arch, Peaks, Pyramid, Fortress, Butterfly, Bridge, and Cross are
        solvable by construction when dealt. The Daily deal rotates across all
        eight; your choices during play can still leave you needing a hint,
        Undo, or Shuffle.
      </p>
    </article>
    <article>
      <h3>Play at your own pace</h3><p>
        Choose Classic or Burst, with scoring, timed combos and automatic clears
        in Burst. Hints, sound controls, Undo, and Shuffle are built in. Shuffle
        itself can be undone, including after a Burst rescue.
      </p>
    </article>
    <article>
      <h3>Keep a record of your progress</h3><p>
        The Records sheet keeps boards cleared, best Classic times and Burst
        scores, and current and longest Daily streaks on this device.
      </p>
    </article>
    <article>
      <h3>Continue an unfinished board</h3><p>
        Blanc remembers your last board, mode, and deal choice. A new Mahjong
        tab can offer to continue an unfinished game from another tab.
      </p>
    </article>
  </div>
</section>

<aside class="truth-note" aria-labelledby="start-page-note-title">
  <h2 id="start-page-note-title">
    Your game and frequent sites stay on this device.
  </h2>
  <p>
    Mahjong games, records, and streaks are not cloud-synced. Billboard’s
    ranking, cached artwork, and hidden tiles also stay local. Your choice among
    the four start-page layouts can sync through Personal’s optional Sync. If
    you enable usage measurement, Blanc can count fixed layout names and the
    first real Mahjong move per app session, without game state or browsing
    data; private-tab feature activity is excluded.
  </p>
  <a
    class="text-link"
    href="/privacy"
    data-track="feature_cta_click"
    data-feature="start-page"
    data-cta-position="related-feature"
    >Read the data details <span aria-hidden="true">↗</span></a
  >
</aside>
